ts, approximately 44 hours of usable data were recorded. This dataset serves as an essential resource for researchers determining oxygen deficiency thresholds in pilots operating under high-altitude flight conditions.</p>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 6775322, "created_date": "2025-10-23T02:07:26Z", "modified_date": "2025-12-09T12:26:31Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["high-altitude flight", "SpO\u2082", "Respiratory", "human"], "keywords": ["high-altitude flight", "SpO\u2082", "Respiratory", "human"], "categories": [{"id": 24715, "title": "Human biophysics", "parent_id": 24709, "path": "/24457/24709/24715", "source_id": "320802", "taxonomy_id": 100}], "references": [], "has_linked_file": false, "citation": "jia, chunyang (2025). High-Altitude Pilot Physiological Monitoring Dataset: Respiratory Performance and SpO\u2082 Analysis. figshare. Dataset. https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.29947679.v1", "related_materials": [], "is_embargoed": false, "embargo_date": null, "embargo_type": null, "embargo_title": "", "embargo_reason": "", "embargo_options": [], "id": 29947679, "title": "High-Altitude Pilot Physiological Monitoring Dataset: Respiratory Performance and SpO\u2082 Analysis", "doi": "10.6084/m9.figshare.29947679.v1", "handle": "", "url": "https://api.figshare.com/v2/articles/29947679", "published_date": "2025-10-23T02:07:26Z", "thumb": "", "defined_type": 3, "defined_type_name": "dataset", "group_id": null, "url_private_api": "https://api.figshare.com/v2/account/articles/29947679", "url_public_api": "https://api.figshare.com/v2/articles/29947679", "url_private_html": "https://figshare.com/account/articles/29947679", "url_public_html": "https://figshare.com/articles/dataset/High-Altitude_Pilot_Physiological_Monit